so many directions to take,

01:01:55.985 --> 01:01:58.370
and I think you did a beautiful
job kind of communicating,

01:01:58.370 --> 01:02:01.730
not just the topic, but the
topic through your work,

01:02:01.730 --> 01:02:04.066
which is, I think was
really quite impressive

01:02:04.066 --> 01:02:06.120
how you've been able to address it.

01:02:06.120 --> 01:02:07.790
We're gonna start with
something invariably,

01:02:07.790 --> 01:02:10.400
you've thought about
with regards to the way

01:02:10.400 --> 01:02:13.180
that we address this problem
in contemporary settings.

01:02:13.180 --> 01:02:16.030
There's this notion that we are just going

01:02:16.030 --> 01:02:19.310
to add more data to the
problem and we will solve it.

01:02:19.310 --> 01:02:22.270
We seek more genomes and more
genomes and more genomes,

01:02:22.270 --> 01:02:24.180
or perhaps a little more charitably

01:02:24.180 --> 01:02:27.580
we get more diverse genomes
for more diverse backgrounds.

01:02:27.580 --> 01:02:29.940
And I think when, if we
understand more and more genomes,

01:02:29.940 --> 01:02:32.840
we'll kind of solve the problem that way.

01:02:32.840 --> 01:02:35.220
And obviously some people who like

01:02:35.220 --> 01:02:37.670
when respects even take that approach,

01:02:37.670 --> 01:02:40.060
maybe even on thinking about
the problem in a humane way,

01:02:40.060 --> 01:02:41.410
as you would articulate it.

01:02:42.380 --> 01:02:43.772
I want you to respond to that.

01:02:43.772 --> 01:02:46.360
What is your take on that
approach to these problems?

01:02:46.360 --> 01:02:48.530
- Okay. So Brian, which mic am I using?

01:02:48.530 --> 01:02:49.423
Not the...

01:02:50.269 --> 01:02:51.440
This one, right?

01:02:51.440 --> 01:02:52.273
- Yeah.

01:02:52.273 --> 01:02:54.380
- All right. So I can take this one off.

01:02:54.380 --> 01:02:57.120
So to answer your question Brandon and

01:03:00.204 --> 01:03:05.090
I think there are some cases...

01:03:14.900 --> 01:03:19.053
There's some cases where we
might need more data, (chuckles)

01:03:19.896 --> 01:03:24.192
but I wouldn't say we need
more genomic data. (chuckles)

01:03:24.192 --> 01:03:28.770
I would say we need more of
the other data. (chuckles)

01:03:28.770 --> 01:03:32.000
But we need more genomic
data on some things.

01:03:32.000 --> 01:03:34.377
There's some things where,

01:03:34.377 --> 01:03:36.680
and when I say some things,

01:03:36.680 --> 01:03:41.680
there's some issues where
we don't need anymore data,

01:03:41.770 --> 01:03:44.680
we don't need any more data, I think,

01:03:44.680 --> 01:03:46.970
and someone argue with me to tell us

01:03:46.970 --> 01:03:48.953
that humans don't have biological race.

01:03:49.820 --> 01:03:52.033
There are people who
say, well, what if we,

01:03:52.033 --> 01:03:55.120
because we often say
humans are young species.

01:03:55.120 --> 01:03:56.217
We haven't lived long enough to have,

01:03:56.217 --> 01:03:58.200
and people say, well, what if we look

01:03:58.200 --> 01:04:00.540
for a million years from now?

01:04:00.540 --> 01:04:03.860
Well, we might have some biological areas.

01:04:03.860 --> 01:04:06.600
We'll think about that then, right now,

01:04:06.600 --> 01:04:07.450
we don't have it.

01:04:08.480 --> 01:04:10.560
So in terms of that issue and

01:04:10.560 --> 01:04:13.560
how we understand human genetic variation

01:04:13.560 --> 01:04:17.320
and human variation, there's
a lot we can understand

01:04:17.320 --> 01:04:18.900
about human still

01:04:18.900 --> 01:04:22.540
to be understood with
regard to human variation.

01:04:22.540 --> 01:04:26.168
But with regard to the issue of race,

01:04:26.168 --> 01:04:30.350
I think we have the
information we need right now.

01:04:30.350 --> 01:04:32.990
The information that tells us
about our common human origin,

01:04:32.990 --> 01:04:36.230
the emotion tells us
about frequency and all,

01:04:36.230 --> 01:04:38.080
I think we have enough

01:04:39.042 --> 01:04:43.600
to drive home those messages
to people who don't know.

01:04:43.600 --> 01:04:46.120
I'm not naive enough to think,

01:04:46.120 --> 01:04:47.770
and even in teaching
race genomics in society,

01:04:47.770 --> 01:04:49.870
I'm not naive enough to
think that just giving people

01:04:49.870 --> 01:04:51.180
that information is gonna take care

01:04:51.180 --> 01:04:52.957
of the racism problem.

01:04:52.957 --> 01:04:56.920
It's not in and of itself is
gonna take care of the racism,

01:04:56.920 --> 01:04:58.680
but it has a role to play.

01:04:58.680 --> 01:05:00.710
In our national survey that I showed you,

01:05:00.710 --> 01:05:03.760
54% of the US population believe

01:05:03.760 --> 01:05:05.420
that there're biological races.

01:05:05.420 --> 01:05:07.360
What they understand by biological races,

01:05:07.360 --> 01:05:10.259
we didn't get into that, but we will,

01:05:10.259 --> 01:05:15.259
but the ideas that surround
that knowledge are important.

01:05:19.910 --> 01:05:21.720
And so helping people understand

01:05:24.630 --> 01:05:26.370
how we are related to each other

01:05:26.370 --> 01:05:31.320
as humans is important,
is still important,

01:05:31.320 --> 01:05:33.840
but we have a lot more
work to do in society.

01:05:33.840 --> 01:05:35.667
But I think it's gonna
take the geneticists

01:05:35.667 --> 01:05:38.320
and the social scientists and
all of us working together

01:05:38.320 --> 01:05:41.143
to solve the racism problem.

01:05:42.070 --> 01:05:45.130
Collecting more genetic
data and genomic data

01:05:45.130 --> 01:05:46.640
can tell us something.

01:05:46.640 --> 01:05:48.170
But I think in the end,

01:05:48.170 --> 01:05:52.950
we need to collect more
data on the context

01:05:52.950 --> 01:05:55.210
within which genes operate

01:05:55.210 --> 01:05:57.650
to help us understand this complexity.

01:05:57.650 --> 01:06:02.650
And context broadly defined,
not just what we eat,

01:06:02.654 --> 01:06:06.490
but the racism that affects
us and influences our health

01:06:06.490 --> 01:06:09.560
and help us understand how
those stressors interact

01:06:09.560 --> 01:06:13.070
with genetic or other
factors to influence that.

01:06:13.070 --> 01:06:15.730
That complexity we don't understand fully

01:06:15.730 --> 01:06:18.789
and we are not even close
to understanding it.

01:06:18.789 --> 01:06:21.153
So in that case for that,
I think we need more data.

